{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgw8azEvEKAcHrhesWUfB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Tq7u6ZWGQpQaaLQMoMuqaD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\np='paper.tex'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"The sealed evaluation used 680 episodes (500 main and 180 control) and took 1400 seconds of the 5400-second budget. % @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes]]\"\nassert old in s\nnew=\"The sealed evaluation plan declares 100 draws for each of five families (500 main episodes) plus 30 draws for each of two base pools and three control types (180 control episodes), 680 in total (constants \\\\texttt{REPS\\\\_MAIN} and \\\\texttt{REPS\\\\_CONTROL} in \\\\texttt{source\\\\_evidence/evaluate\\\\_final.py}). The five recorded partitions have durations that sum to about 1332 seconds, against a wall-clock limit of 5400 seconds in the same script. % @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py]] @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes]]\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new))\nc=open('claims_grounding.json').read()\no=\"Sealed evaluation: 680 episodes (500 main, 180 control), 100 draws per family, n=500 N=20000 on real pools, 1400 s elapsed\"\nassert o in c\nc=c.replace(o,\"Sealed evaluation plan: 680 episodes (500 main = 100 draws x 5 families; 180 control = 30 draws x 2 base pools x 3 control types) per REPS_MAIN/REPS_CONTROL in source_evidence/evaluate_final.py lines 62-63 and 439-446; five recorded partition durations sum to about 1332 s (265.5-267.2 s each) against a 5400 s wall-clock limit (WALL_SECONDS, evaluate_final.py line 73)\")\nopen('claims_grounding.json','w').write(c)\nE\ngrep -rn \"source_evidence\" paper.tex | head -5; ls scientific-evidence/schemas | head; grep -n \"evidence\\[\\[source_evidence\\|evidence\\[\\[analysis\" paper.tex | head -3"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1116,"cache_read_input_tokens":48105,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1116},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47c0712e-4fb3-4bc4-89cb-dde44d1b3be8","uuid":"b63365a1-2d29-44a0-95e8-a3e4ddc33957","timestamp":"2026-11-11T12:21:33.253Z","request_id":"req_011Cgw8aycTx6xGZa6PgxCh3"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tq7u6ZWGQpQaaLQMoMuqaD","type":"tool_result","content":"paper.tex:203:The recalibrated variant is largest on the synthetic family (0.0757) and gene expression (0.0290), and smallest on galaxy morphology (0.0035). % @evidence[[source_evidence/search_metrics/recalibrated_metrics.json]]\npaper.tex:204:The stacked variant tracks it on the synthetic family (0.0707) and gene expression (0.0278) but is smaller on deforestation and protein disorder; the smooth label-free basis is close to PPI++ on the synthetic family (0.0034), where the nonlinearity is the exponential regime of the search generator. % @evidence[[source_evidence/search_metrics/stacked_metrics.json]] @evidence[[source_evidence/search_metrics/label_free_basis_metrics.json]]\npaper.tex:205:Search-pool pooled coverage was 0.943 for the recalibrated and the stacked variants and 0.950 for the basis variant, with minimum family coverage 0.933, 0.917 and 0.933 respectively. % @evidence[[source_evidence/search_metrics/recalibrated_metrics.json]] @evidence[[source_evidence/search_metrics/stacked_metrics.json]] @evidence[[source_evidence/search_metrics/label_free_basis_metrics.json]]\npaper.tex:274:% @evidence[[source_evidence/search_metrics/recalibrated_metrics.json]] @evidence[[source_evidence/search_metrics/stacked_metrics.json]] @evidence[[source_evidence/search_metrics/label_free_basis_metrics.json]]\npaper.tex:277:Search pools: galaxy morphology (Galaxy Zoo-type crowd labels, \\citealt{Willett2013GalaxyZ2}; $n=300$, $N=5000$), Amazon deforestation ($n=100$, $N=1000$), gene expression ($n=500$, $N=10000$), protein disorder ($n=300$, $N=5000$), and synthetic regimes, 60 draws per family, reset seeds 1001--1005. We cite an original data source only for the galaxy and census pools; the original sources of the plankton, deforestation, gene-expression and protein-disorder pools were not traced for this paper. The sealed evaluation plan declares 100 draws for each of five families (500 main episodes) plus 30 draws for each of two base pools and three control types (180 control episodes), 680 in total (constants \\texttt{REPS\\_MAIN} and \\texttt{REPS\\_CONTROL} in \\texttt{source\\_evidence/evaluate\\_final.py}). The five recorded partitions have durations that sum to about 1332 seconds, against a wall-clock limit of 5400 seconds in the same script. % @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py]] @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes]]\nartifact-manifest.schema.json\nevidence-reference.schema.json\nledger-entry.schema.json\nverification-report.schema.json\n129:Both point estimates lie below the nominal 0.95. Under exact binomial calculations with $p=0.95$, the lower-tail probabilities of the observed counts are 0.066 (pooled) and 0.063 (lowest family), % @evidence[[analysis/headroom_derived.json#coverage]]\n130:which is why the gate did not reject, but also not strong support for exact nominal coverage; the Monte Carlo standard errors are 0.011 and 0.029. % @evidence[[analysis/headroom_derived.json#coverage]]\n136:Most of the gain over labeled-only inference is therefore already captured by PPI machinery; recalibration adds a small increment on top. Per family, the narrowing against PPI++ is 0.0287 for census income, 0.0018 for census insurance, 0.0023 for census education, 0.0359 for plankton and 0.0413 for the synthetic mixture, corresponding to derived width reductions of 2.8\\%, 0.2\\%, 0.2\\%, 3.5\\% and 4.0\\%. % @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.metrics]] @evidence[[analysis/headroom_derived.json#derived_width_reduction_vs_ppi_pp]]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47c0712e-4fb3-4bc4-89cb-dde44d1b3be8","uuid":"55805890-ff17-4705-9740-60929d39738a","timestamp":"2026-11-11T12:21:33.366Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"paper.tex:203:The recalibrated variant is largest on the synthetic family (0.0757) and gene expression (0.0290), an